## 5. API Routes

### 5.1 Auth Routes (delegated to better-auth)

```
POST /api/auth/sign-up/email
POST /api/auth/sign-in/email
POST /api/auth/sign-out
GET  /api/auth/session
POST /api/auth/verify-email
POST /api/auth/forget-password
POST /api/auth/reset-password
```

Mount with: `app.all("/api/auth/*", (req, res) => auth.handler(req, res))`

### 5.2 Onboarding

```
POST /api/onboarding/role          — set role (mentor|mentee), create profile row
POST /api/onboarding/mentor        — save mentor profile fields
POST /api/onboarding/mentee        — save mentee profile fields
POST /api/onboarding/complete      — mark onboarding_complete = true
```

**Middleware:** `requireAuth` on all. After `POST /complete`, update `users.onboarding_complete = true` via better-auth's `updateUser`.

### 5.3 Mentor Profiles

```
GET  /api/mentors                  — paginated list, filters: tags, verified, name search
GET  /api/mentors/:mentorId        — public profile + reviews
GET  /api/mentors/me               — own profile (auth required)
PUT  /api/mentors/me               — update own profile (auth + role=mentor)
```

**Query params for list:** `page`, `limit`, `tags` (comma-separated), `verified`, `search`, `sort` (rating|sessions|newest).

**Cache:** `GET /api/mentors` and `GET /api/mentors/:id` use cache before hitting DB.

### 5.4 Availability

```
GET  /api/availability/:mentorId           — weekly slots + booked times
PUT  /api/availability                     — mentor sets their weekly recurring slots
GET  /api/availability/:mentorId/open      — open slots for a given week (?weekStart=ISO)
```

`GET /open` computes: recurring slots for that week - sessions already booked in that range.

### 5.5 Sessions

```
POST   /api/sessions                — mentee books a session (creates Daily room)
GET    /api/sessions                — own sessions (mentor sees all theirs, mentee sees theirs)
GET    /api/sessions/:sessionId     — session detail (auth + participant)
PATCH  /api/sessions/:sessionId/confirm   — mentor confirms (status: pending → confirmed)
PATCH  /api/sessions/:sessionId/cancel   — either party cancels
PATCH  /api/sessions/:sessionId/complete — mark completed (auto via webhook or cron)
GET    /api/sessions/:sessionId/join     — returns meeting_url (only within 10min of start)
```

**Booking flow (`POST /api/sessions`):**

1. Validate slot is still open (check DB, race-condition safe with SQLite exclusive transaction)
2. Create Daily.co room via `POST https://api.daily.co/v1/rooms` with `exp` set to `scheduled_at + duration + 30min`
3. Insert session row with `status: 'pending'`
4. Send notification to mentor
5. Return session object

**Daily.co room creation:**

```ts
const room = await fetch('https://api.daily.co/v1/rooms', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.DAILY_API_KEY}`,
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    name: `mentorship-${sessionId}`,
    privacy: 'private',
    properties: {
      exp: Math.floor(scheduledAtUnix + durationSecs + 1800),
      max_participants: 2,
      enable_chat: true,
      enable_screenshare: false,
    },
  }),
})
```

### 5.6 Reviews

```
POST /api/reviews               — mentee submits review (session must be completed)
GET  /api/reviews/:mentorId     — public reviews for a mentor (paginated)
```

After `POST /api/reviews`, update `mentor_profiles.avg_rating` and `review_count` atomically.

### 5.7 Notifications

```
GET    /api/notifications         — own notifications (paginated, newest first)
PATCH  /api/notifications/read    — mark all as read
PATCH  /api/notifications/:id/read — mark one as read
```

### 5.8 Admin

```
GET    /api/admin/verification-requests           — list pending requests
PATCH  /api/admin/verification-requests/:id       — approve/reject
GET    /api/admin/users                           — list all users
GET    /api/admin/stats                           — platform stats
PATCH  /api/admin/mentors/:mentorId/suspend       — suspend mentor
```

All admin routes: `requireAuth` + `requireRole('admin')`.

---

## 6. Middleware Stack

```ts
app.use(cors({ origin: process.env.FRONTEND_URL, credentials: true }))
app.use(express.json())
app.use(helmet())
app.use(rateLimit({ windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, max: 100 })) // per IP
```

**Custom middleware:**

```ts
// requireAuth.ts
export async function requireAuth(req, res, next) {
  const session = await auth.api.getSession({ headers: req.headers })
  if (!session) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' })
  req.session = session
  req.user = session.user
  next()
}

// requireRole.ts
export function requireRole(...roles: string[]) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    if (!roles.includes(req.user.role))
      return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' })
    next()
  }
}

// requireOnboarding.ts — redirect if not onboarded
export function requireOnboarding(req, res, next) {
  if (!req.user.onboardingComplete) {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'ONBOARDING_REQUIRED' })
  }
  next()
}
```

---

## 7. Background Jobs (simple setInterval, no queue lib)

```ts
// jobs.ts — start on server boot

// 1. Session reminder notifications (runs every 5 min)
// Finds sessions scheduled in next 24h with no reminder sent → create notification
setInterval(sendSessionReminders, 5 * 60 * 1000)

// 2. Auto-complete sessions (runs every 10 min)
// Sessions where scheduled_at + duration has passed and status = 'confirmed' → mark 'completed'
setInterval(autoCompleteSessions, 10 * 60 * 1000)

// 3. Cache cleanup (runs every 30 min)
// Any expired entries not yet evicted
setInterval(() => cache.cleanup(), 30 * 60 * 1000)
```

